        <briefdescription>
<para>Convert a double to a string. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Internal helper. The output matches the former ostk::core::type::Real::toString(precision) output, except that NaN prints as &quot;NaN&quot; (there is no undefined double): infinities print as &quot;+Inf&quot; / &quot;-Inf&quot;. With a negative precision, integral values keep a trailing &quot;.0&quot;, and other values use the round-trip representation without trailing zeros. With a non-negative precision, fixed notation with that many decimals is used.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespaceostk_1_1physics_1_1utility_1ac39c8de8825eafee30b07310c43fe237" kindref="member">DoubleToString</ref>(1.0)<sp/>;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>&quot;1.0&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespaceostk_1_1physics_1_1utility_1ac39c8de8825eafee30b07310c43fe237" kindref="member">DoubleToString</ref>(0.5)<sp/>;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>&quot;0.5&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="namespaceostk_1_1physics_1_1utility_1ac39c8de8825eafee30b07310c43fe237" kindref="member">DoubleToString</ref>(0.5,<sp/>3)<sp/>;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>&quot;0.500&quot;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
